<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    NEW. This def is not SyndicateGamingNetwork's - the texture is.

    AB_AirConditioner.png shipped in the original mod, finished, 64x64, and no def declared it.
    It is the only piece of art in there that the game never loaded: a rusted condenser seen
    from above, a fan in a round housing over a vent grille. This file gives it the building it
    was drawn for. It lives apart from AB_Buildings_Structure.xml so that the boundary between
    what was ported and what was added is visible in the file listing, not only in the comments.

    The design follows the other four rather than inventing a new idea. Every building in this
    mod is a cheaper, cruder variant of something vanilla already has - a concrete fence beside
    the fence, a barrier beside the sandbags, a one-tile stove beside the three-tile one - and
    each pays for what it saves. So this is a cooler: the same machine, in the same place in the
    tech tree, cheaper and quicker to put up, and thirstier and weaker once it runs.

                                   vanilla cooler   this
      steel / components                 90 / 3     70 / 2
      work to build                        1600     1200
      construction skill                      5        4
      power                                200W     250W
      cooling (energyPerSecond)             -21      -16

    It is deliberately NOT free of the research. AirConditioning is a real progression gate -
    it is what stands between a colony and a walk-in freezer - and handing it over for the price
    of one mod would change the game rather than furnish it. The rest of this mod asks for no
    research because none of it unlocks anything; this would.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>AB_AirConditioner</defName>
    <label>ancient air conditioner</label>
    <description>A salvaged air-cooling unit that fits into a wall. Cool air comes out one side, while hot exhaust comes out the other. Older and cruder than a modern cooler: it drinks more power and moves less heat, but it is quicker to put together out of less.</description>
    <thingClass>Building_Cooler</thingClass>
    <graphicData>
      <!--
        Graphic_Single, because there is one texture and only one. That is not a shortcut: a
        Graphic_Single on a rotatable building is drawn turned to face its rotation, so the
        grille swings round with the unit and goes on marking the exhaust side, which is the
        one thing about a cooler a player has to be able to read at a glance.
      -->
      <texPath>Things/Building/ABSingle/AB_AirConditioner</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <damageData>
        <cornerTL>Damage/Corner</cornerTL>
        <cornerTR>Damage/Corner</cornerTR>
        <cornerBL>Damage/Corner</cornerBL>
        <cornerBR>Damage/Corner</cornerBR>
      </damageData>
    </graphicData>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <blockWind>true</blockWind>
    <fillPercent>1</fillPercent>
    <coversFloor>true</coversFloor>
    <blockLight>true</blockLight>
    <canOverlapZones>false</canOverlapZones>
    <castEdgeShadows>true</castEdgeShadows>
    <blockWeather>true</blockWeather>
    <staticSunShadowHeight>1.0</staticSunShadowHeight>
    <statBases>
      <WorkToBuild>1200</WorkToBuild>
      <MaxHitPoints>100</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.7</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <tickerType>Rare</tickerType>
    <costList>
      <Steel>70</Steel>
      <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
    </costList>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Medium</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <placeWorkers>
      <li>PlaceWorker_Cooler</li>
    </placeWorkers>
    <drawPlaceWorkersWhileSelected>true</drawPlaceWorkersWhileSelected>
    <!--
      isAirtight and canPlaceOverWall are what make this a wall unit rather than a box in the
      middle of a room, and they are not decoration: Building_Cooler reads the room on the cold
      side and the room on the hot side. Set in the open, both cells are the same room and the
      machine does nothing at all but draw power.
    -->
    <building>
      <canPlaceOverWall>true</canPlaceOverWall>
      <isAirtight>true</isAirtight>
    </building>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Power">
        <compClass>CompPowerTrader</compClass>
        <basePowerConsumption>250</basePowerConsumption>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Flickable" />
      <li Class="CompProperties_TempControl">
        <energyPerSecond>-16</energyPerSecond>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Breakdownable" />
    </comps>
    <designationCategory>Temperature</designationCategory>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>AirConditioning</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <constructionSkillPrerequisite>4</constructionSkillPrerequisite>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
